cxu|n|Pertaining to a city or state, or to a citizen in his relations to his fellow citizens or to the state; within the city or state. ; Subject to government; reduced to order; civilized; not barbarous; -- said of the community. ; Performing the duties of a citizen; obedient to government; -- said of an individual. ; Having the manners of one dwelling in a city, as opposed to those of savages or rustics; polite; courteous; complaisant; affable. ; Pertaining to civic life and affairs, in distinction from military, ecclesiastical, or official state. ; Relating to rights and remedies sought by action or suit distinct from criminal proceedings.	V:obz,4,1~obz,4,1	N:2810,51,7;obx,33,2;obz,4,1~2810,51,7;obx,33,2;obz,4,1
